ATTRIBUTION CONFIRMED:
- A MIXED batch (own + foreign ids) is rejected by the NEW zone gate — the warning fires,
  and it names exactly the 2 FOREIGN ids, not the attacker's own in-zone id. The gate
  discriminates correctly.
- An ALL-FOREIGN batch is short-circuited earlier by the OLD doesntExist() check (which is
  itself ZoneScope'd, so a batch with zero in-zone ids makes that aggregate true). AC2 holds,
  but it is guarded by the pre-existing check, not by the new gate — the engineer's test
  docblock states this honestly rather than overclaiming.
- Presence of the warning => new gate. Absence + rejection => old gate. Distinguishable.

LOG PII-SAFETY (docs/platform/logging-contract.md — ids-only allow-list):
  payload = {"item_ids":[...], "admin_id":N}
  ids ONLY. No CSV row bodies. No request payloads. No tokens. No names/phones/addresses.
  PASS. Consistent with the sibling Log::warning lines already in this controller
  (:1437, :1443, :1563, :1569).

EXISTENCE-ORACLE CONTAINMENT (conductor decision: message must be GENERIC, must not name ids):
  $foreign_ids appears in the Log::warning line ONLY. It is never passed to Toastr, never
  interpolated into the response. Verified by grep over the gate block :1607-1619.
